                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2cb159fc-823f-3f4d-a7ff-22fe33cf9064",
                        "entry_id": "643a3b28-afe1-3cca-a171-f7391a19426e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. недостаток мужества, твёрдости духа, веры и решительности"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7ade66c-ab93-4d12-8b46-a97c685d27d1",
                                "sense_id": "2cb159fc-823f-3f4d-a7ff-22fe33cf9064",
                                "text": "Только теперь вижу ясно всю нелепость моего малодушия, теперь, как уж решился идти на этот ненужный стыд!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03fc61ba-0191-4d50-adad-7c722fb6dd18",
                                "sense_id": "2cb159fc-823f-3f4d-a7ff-22fe33cf9064",
                                "text": "Он говорил прекрасно, горячо, убедительно — о позоре малодушия и лени, о необходимости делать дело."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "378fa9df-2cce-40ef-b3e5-6096f0cd6580",
                                "sense_id": "2cb159fc-823f-3f4d-a7ff-22fe33cf9064",
                                "text": "Это даже уж не загадка, а какое-то колдовство, которое я назвал бы историческим, если б не боялся, чтоб этот эпитет не послужил прикрытием для всякого рода малодуший."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "311c100c-cabb-4582-ae63-5283585c159d",
                        "source_entry_id": "643a3b28-afe1-3cca-a171-f7391a19426e",
                        "source_sense_id": "2cb159fc-823f-3f4d-a7ff-22fe33cf9064",
                        "target_lang_word": "faintheartedness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "faintheartedness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5ae2fc2-355e-32ec-9dbf-912edc9c4ee0",
                                        "entry_id": "9fcb25df-7bdd-352e-9c46-14e463b1fe9d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality or state of being fainthearted."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71ce5118-335b-49f3-a7f4-f3d6c411c66b",
                                                "sense_id": "d5ae2fc2-355e-32ec-9dbf-912edc9c4ee0",
                                                "text": "1899, Dante Gabriel Rossetti (transl.), The New Life (La Vita Nuova) of Dante Alighieri, Siddall edition, pages 77-78.\nIn the third, I say what it is I purpose to speak so as not to be impeded by faintheartedness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f7c0e138-971a-4bbe-9a6e-f3f0d6deabdf",
                        "source_entry_id": "643a3b28-afe1-3cca-a171-f7391a19426e",
                        "source_sense_id": "2cb159fc-823f-3f4d-a7ff-22fe33cf9064",
                        "target_lang_word": "cowardice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cowardice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5209ddb0-b90a-340e-8e35-2bcf25c97319",
                                        "entry_id": "f6938660-b95b-375a-ae2c-78a7356dc459",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lack of courage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae1eea65-3152-4a5a-a0ae-1ef84bf43a12",
                                                "sense_id": "5209ddb0-b90a-340e-8e35-2bcf25c97319",
                                                "text": "The ſecond property of your excellent ſherris, is the vvarming of the blood, vvhich before (cold & ſetled) left the lyuer vvhite & pale, vvhich is the badge of puſilanimitie and covvardize: but the ſherris vvarmes it, and makes it courſe from the invvards to the partes extreames, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f804cd3-2589-4bf6-8f2e-55c6188ae2e9",
                                                "sense_id": "5209ddb0-b90a-340e-8e35-2bcf25c97319",
                                                "text": "[Ilhan] Omar was left twisting in the wind earlier this year after facing spurious charges of antisemitism, a display of Democratic cowardice co-signed by Chelsea Clinton, Chuck Schumer, and most every other Democrat with a congressional leadership position."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "00ff5b28-6916-4369-8c3c-381df1aee978",
                        "source_entry_id": "643a3b28-afe1-3cca-a171-f7391a19426e",
                        "source_sense_id": "2cb159fc-823f-3f4d-a7ff-22fe33cf9064",
                        "target_lang_word": "pusillanimity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pusillanimity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f65a8a7e-7de3-3dfa-89a3-8cb65fc7eed6",
                                        "entry_id": "cc1f1663-4d3c-34da-b70b-34fd66a6279e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality or state of being pusillanimous; the vice of being timid and cowardly, and thus not living up to one's full potential; pusillanimousness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ceeebd1-08bb-4c44-98c3-0823e3fdc816",
                                                "sense_id": "f65a8a7e-7de3-3dfa-89a3-8cb65fc7eed6",
                                                "text": "The ſecond property of your excellent ſherris, is the vvarming of the blood, vvhich before (cold & ſetled) left the lyuer vvhite & pale, vvhich is the badge of puſilanimitie and covvardize: but the ſherris vvarmes it, and makes it courſe from the invvards to the partes extreames, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7a64384-61ae-4d04-9e50-f1d391379064",
                                                "sense_id": "f65a8a7e-7de3-3dfa-89a3-8cb65fc7eed6",
                                                "text": "[…] Puſillanimity; by vvhich that ſeems great to him, vvhich other men think a trifle: and vvhatſoever is nevv, or great, and therefore thought fit to be told, vvithdravves a man by degrees from the intended vvay of his diſcourſe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80a0a797-091a-47e2-bbda-9424f11876ce",
                                                "sense_id": "f65a8a7e-7de3-3dfa-89a3-8cb65fc7eed6",
                                                "text": "1685. Dr. Michael de Molinos: The Spiritual Guide which Disentangles the Soul, and Brings it by the Inward Way To The Getting of Perfect Contemplation and the Rich Treasure of Internal Peace, CHAP. XVIII: http://www.ccel.org/ccel/molinos/guide.html.\n132. And although thou often fallest, and seest thy Pusillanimity, and endeavour to get courage, and afflict not thy self; because what God doth not do in forty Years, he sometimes doth in an instant, with a particular Mystery, that we may live low and humble, and know that ‘tis the Work of his powerful Hand, to free us from Sins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8dcf071-c84c-4702-b0d3-facb3ffafe17",
                                                "sense_id": "f65a8a7e-7de3-3dfa-89a3-8cb65fc7eed6",
                                                "text": "Instead of being confined within the walls of fortified cities, which the Romans considered as the refuge of weakness or pusillanimity, the legions were encamped on the banks of the great rivers, and along the frontiers of the barbarians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a67defb-3b60-4c37-9adc-d136fac36a98",
                                                "sense_id": "f65a8a7e-7de3-3dfa-89a3-8cb65fc7eed6",
                                                "text": "their hectorings against an absent enemy, and their pusillanimity on his approach"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb9ab355-048a-47ee-ad9f-7a2b7ec407bd",
                                                "sense_id": "f65a8a7e-7de3-3dfa-89a3-8cb65fc7eed6",
                                                "text": "What I did through indolence and in some degree, I confess, through pusillanimity, I had a fancy to make it appear (by dint of much whistling, as it were, and easy thrusting of my hands into my pocket) that I did through a sort of generous condescension."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
